--- body ---
## Context
`docs/portable-model-capability-policy.md` (PR #1002) replaces concrete Claude
tier names in portable skills with two semantic controls — `model-level`
(`auto | cheap | standard | strong | frontier`) and `effort`
(`economy | standard | intensive`) — resolved by per-runtime adapters. It
proposes six phases (0–5); this tracker owns the sequence. Children are filed
one phase at a time, each `Blocked-by` its predecessor, never this tracker.

Blast radius: `rules/claude-code.md` § Subagent levers,
`tests/test_model_rightsizing.py`, `agents/team-lead.md`, and every fan-out in
`skills/` (`raid`, `hunt`, `gaze`, review and audit). Phases 3 and 5 touch many
of these at once and will need their own decomposition when reached.

Open design points to settle inside the phases, not before:
- team lead effort: `standard` by default; `economy` only if Phase 5 traces
  show verification quality holds (doc § Default role policy).
- `decorrelated-from` resolution rule per adapter (invariant 5).

## Children
- 0975 — Phase 0: vocabulary + behaviour-preserving Claude mapping
  (closed 2026-09-25; accepted with sandbox-only full-gate failures waived;
  see `tickets/closed/0975-phase-0-semantic-model-level-and-effort.erg`)
- 1000 — skill compute intentions made portable (autoclosed by PR #1092,
  2026-10-01; retroactive child). Skills declare `model-level`/`effort` in
  prose and carry no concrete model names; no pins remain to agree with, so
  Phases 1 and 3 are delivered in a different shape than the doc planned.
  Covered invariants: 2, 3, 4, 9 (`tests/test_model_policy.py`,
  `tests/test_model_rightsizing.py`); 4 and 9 waived 2026-10-06 and
  `tests/test_model_policy.py` removed, see the inventory below.

## Remaining (2026-10-05 audit)
Uncovered invariants: 1 (no silent inheritance on broad fan-out), 5
(`decorrelated-from`), 6 (`intensive` never default for broad fan-out), 7
(provider mechanics), 8 (trace recording). Phase 4 is largely retired by the
2026-10-01 decision that the runtime, not the harness, owns translation: waive
7 in writing or scope it to the Claude mapping only. Phase 2 (`team-lead`
profile) and Phase 5 (economic defaults) are unfiled; Phase 5 waits on the
1024 tournament measurements. No child is filed until a gap clears the
severity floor.

## Invariant inventory (2026-10-06, read-only; suite not run)
Invariants are numbered as in `docs/portable-model-capability-policy.md`
§ Tests and invariants. "Evidence" names what a reader can open. Dispositions
for 4, 6, 7, 8, 9 were decided by the author on 2026-10-06 (see log).

| # | Evidence found | State | Disposition |
|---|----------------|-------|-------------|
| 1 | `test_fanout_skill_bodies_declare_model_level` checks that a fan-out skill body declares a level; it does not observe a launch | partial | keep as text-level cover; real launch cover belongs to the runtime adapter |
| 2 | same test, plus `test_skill_compute_frontmatter_is_semantic` | covered | none |
| 3 | `test_portable_skill_instructions_do_not_name_models` and its negative control | covered | none |
| 4 | `test_invalid_intentions_fail_explicitly` exercised `ClaudeMapping`, which no live code called | waived 2026-10-06 | author choice C: the harness holds no translation code; removed with its tests |
| 5 | `decorrelated-from` is declared in `skills/biblio-saturation/SKILL.md` only; `gaze`, `reviewers/references/live-route.md` and `rules/workflow.md` state decorrelation in prose; no resolver, no adapter test | uncovered | open question, nearest to the severity floor; shares the model-id blocker of 1038 on Vibe |
| 6 | `skills/raid/SKILL.md` carried `Requested effort: intensive` in prose, outside frontmatter, contradicting its own body (orchestration `standard/standard`) | resolved 2026-10-06 | author doctrine, two rules: `frontier` is for one-shot calls only, never an orchestrator or fan-out setting; `intensive` is rarely paired with `frontier` (cost) and is not a frontier property. Raid orchestrator set to `standard`, advisor to `frontier`/`standard`; no test (a prose-scanning test is brittle) |
| 7 | no provider-mechanics test; the only mapping test covered `ClaudeMapping`, which no live code called | waived 2026-10-06 | author choice C (2026-10-01 decision: runtime owns translation). Whether Codex and Pi expose model and effort controls was not read |
| 8 | no trace recording of the requested level/effort; `scripts/attribution_record.py` requires `runtime`, `model`, `effort` for the writer line, which covers the concrete result only | attached to Phase 5 | author accepted 2026-10-06: Phase 5 needs traces and waits for 1024 |
| 9 | `test_auto_is_a_configured_tier_not_session_inheritance` exercised `ClaudeMapping`, which no live code called | waived 2026-10-06 | author choice C. Residual risk: nothing executable states that `auto` never resolves to the caller's model; it is rule text (`rules/claude-code.md`) plus the text-level test for invariants 1 and 2 |

Count (2026-10-06): covered 2, 3; partial 1; uncovered 5; waived 4, 7, 9;
resolved 6; attached to Phase 5: 8. The exit criterion "invariants 1–9 backed or
waived" stays open until 5 is settled and 8 lands with Phase 5. Doctrine and
review brief: `docs/2026-10-06-routing-doctrine-brief.md`.

## Open design point: quota-aware routing
From 0980 (2026-10-05): route more aggressively to conserve Claude Pro Max,
ChatGPT Pro and Vibe Pro quotas; consider the GLM Coding Plan after 1024
(off-peak promotion through 2026-10-07 is half usage credits, not half price;
source docs.z.ai/devpack/overview). Compare an LLM-routing MCP plugin usable
from Claude and Codex against tuning evidence-based IDH routing. No
architecture, provider or purchase selected.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Every phase child closed, and the integration review run per `/roar`
      step 8 (child diffs re-read, full suite, union sweep for leftover
      concrete tier names in portable skills)
- [ ] Doc invariants 1–9 each backed by a test or explicitly waived in writing
- [ ] `make check` passes
